cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this analysis or code, please cite this software release and the associated manuscript."
title: "Bacillales TMD codon positioning analysis"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Li"
    given-names: "Ming"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-05"
repository-code: "https://github.com/daming7977-byte/bacillales-tmd-codon-positioning"
abstract: >
  Reproducibility code and processed results for an independent Bacillales
  analysis of the positional organization of low-adaptation synonymous codon
  segments relative to transmembrane-domain boundaries. The repository includes
  orthology inference, topology qualification, codon-adaptation calculations,
  low-adaptation segment detection, TMD-relative assignment, synonymous-codon
  permutation analysis, supplementary tables, and the Bacillales permutation-null
  figure accompanying the associated manuscript.
keywords:
  - synonymous codon usage
  - transmembrane domains
  - membrane proteins
  - Bacillales
  - molecular evolution
  - permutation test
